{
  "name": "Build a Google Maps lead list in Google Sheets with API.SH",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Build a local business lead list from Google Maps\n\n### How it works\nFill in a short form with a business type, a location, how many result pages to fetch, a minimum rating and whether a website is required. The workflow searches Google Maps with the **API.SH** node (20 places per page), drops closed businesses, duplicates and places below your criteria, then appends the qualified leads to a Google Sheet. The sheet is matched on `place_id`, so running the same search again updates existing leads instead of adding duplicates.\n\n### Setup\n1. Install the verified **API.SH** node (nodes panel → search \"API.SH\") and add your API key from [api.sh](https://api.sh). Each page of 20 places is 1 credit; every account gets 1,000 free credits a month.\n2. Create a Google Sheet with a tab named **Leads** and headers: `place_id`, `name`, `category`, `phone`, `website`, `domain`, `address`, `city`, `rating`, `reviews`, `maps_url`, `search`, `found_at`.\n3. Paste the sheet URL into the Google Sheets node, connect your Google account, activate the workflow and open the form URL.\n\n### Customization\nAdd an enrichment step after the filter (for example a website or email lookup), or replace the form with a schedule and a fixed list of searches.",
        "height": 760,
        "width": 480
      },
      "id": "206e92fc-7e9b-4e94-89cf-faa62774feb2",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
